{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Diffusion Transformers & Rectified Flow Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: A DiT block with AdaLN"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class AdaLNZero(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Adaptive LayerNorm with a gate. Predicts (scale, shift, gate) from the conditioning."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Init such that the whole block starts as identity (\"zero init\")."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, dim, cond_dim):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.norm = nn.LayerNorm(dim, elementwise_affine=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.mlp = nn.Linear(cond_dim, dim * 3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        nn.init.zeros_(self.mlp.weight)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        nn.init.zeros_(self.mlp.bias)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x, cond):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        scale, shift, gate = self.mlp(cond).chunk(3, dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h = self.norm(x) * (1 + scale.unsqueeze(1)) + shift.unsqueeze(1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return h, gate.unsqueeze(1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class DiTBlock(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, dim=192, heads=3, mlp_ratio=4, cond_dim=192):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.adaln1 = AdaLNZero(dim, cond_dim)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.attn = nn.MultiheadAttention(dim, heads, batch_first=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.adaln2 = AdaLNZero(dim, cond_dim)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.mlp = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(dim, dim * mlp_ratio),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.GELU(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(dim * mlp_ratio, dim),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x, cond):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h, gate1 = self.adaln1(x, cond)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        a, _ = self.attn(h, h, h, need_weights=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = x + gate1 * a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h, gate2 = self.adaln2(x, cond)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = x + gate2 * self.mlp(h)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`AdaLNZero` starts as an identity mapping because its MLP weights are initialised to zero. Training nudges the block away from identity; this stabilises deep transformer diffusion models dramatically."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: A tiny DiT"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def timestep_embedding(t, dim):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    half = dim // 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    freqs = torch.exp(-math.log(10000) * torch.arange(half, device=t.device) / half)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    args = t[:, None].float() * freqs[None]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return torch.cat([args.sin(), args.cos()], dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class TinyDiT(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, image_size=16, patch_size=2, in_channels=3, dim=96, depth=4, heads=3):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.patch_size = patch_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.num_patches = (image_size // patch_size) ** 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.patch = nn.Conv2d(in_channels, dim, kernel_size=patch_size, stride=patch_size)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.pos = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(1, self.num_patches, dim))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.time_mlp = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(dim, dim * 2),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.SiLU(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(dim * 2, dim),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.blocks = nn.ModuleList([DiTBlock(dim, heads, cond_dim=dim) for _ in range(depth)])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.norm_out = nn.LayerNorm(dim, elementwise_affine=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.head = nn.Linear(dim, patch_size * patch_size * in_channels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x, t):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n = x.size(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.patch(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = x.flatten(2).transpose(1, 2) + self.pos"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_emb = self.time_mlp(timestep_embedding(t, self.pos.size(-1)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for blk in self.blocks:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            x = blk(x, t_emb)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.norm_out(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.head(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self._unpatchify(x, n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def _unpatchify(self, x, n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        p = self.patch_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h = w = int(self.num_patches ** 0.5)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = x.view(n, h, w, p, p, -1).permute(0, 5, 1, 3, 2, 4).reshape(n, -1, h * p, w * p)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Rectified flow training"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn.functional as F"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def rectified_flow_train_step(model, x0, optimizer, device):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model.train()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x0 = x0.to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = x0.size(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    t = torch.rand(n, device=device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    epsilon = torch.randn_like(x0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x_t = (1 - t[:, None, None, None]) * x0 + t[:, None, None, None] * epsilon"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    target_velocity = epsilon - x0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pred_velocity = model(x_t, t)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = F.mse_loss(pred_velocity, target_velocity)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    optimizer.zero_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    optimizer.step()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return loss.item()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Compare with DDPM's noise-prediction loss (Lesson 10): same structure, different target. Instead of predicting the noise `epsilon`, we predict the **velocity** `epsilon - x_0`, which points from data to noise along the straight-line interpolation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Euler sampler"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Rectified flow is an ODE. Euler's method is the simplest and, for a well-trained rectified-flow model, nearly as accurate as higher-order solvers at 20+ steps."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "@torch.no_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def rectified_flow_sample(model, shape, steps=20, device=\"cpu\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model.eval()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = torch.randn(shape, device=device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dt = 1.0 / steps"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    t = torch.ones(shape[0], device=device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(steps):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        v = model(x, t)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = x - dt * v"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t = t - dt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "20 steps. On a trained model this produces samples comparable to 1000-step DDPM."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: End-to-end smoke test"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def synthetic_blobs(num=200, size=16, seed=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = np.zeros((num, 3, size, size), dtype=np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    yy, xx = np.meshgrid(np.arange(size), np.arange(size), indexing=\"ij\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(num):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        cx, cy = rng.uniform(4, size - 4, size=2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        r = rng.uniform(2, 4)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        mask = (xx - cx) ** 2 + (yy - cy) ** 2 < r ** 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        colour = rng.uniform(-1, 1, size=3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for c in range(3):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            out[i, c][mask] = colour[c]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return torch.from_numpy(out)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Train a `TinyDiT` on this with rectified flow. After 500 steps, sampled outputs should look like faint blobs of colour."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Train the TinyDiT above on the synthetic blob dataset for 500 steps. Compare samples produced with 10, 20, and 50 Euler steps.\n2. **(Medium)** Add text conditioning by concatenating a learned class embedding to the time embedding (10 blob \"classes\" by colour). Sample with class 0, 5, and 9 and verify colours match.\n3. **(Hard)** Compute the Fr\u00e9chet distance (FID proxy) between generated samples from rectified-flow and DDPM versions of the same-size network trained on the same data for the same number of steps. Report which converges faster."
      ]
    }
